<Project>

  <!--
    Drop any Content/None item that points INSIDE the build output, before target paths are
    assigned. This is a guard, not a style choice.

    The SDK tries to exclude the output from its default item globs, but builds those patterns
    from $(BaseOutputPath), whose default is "bin\" — with a Windows separator. On macOS and
    Linux a backslash is an ordinary filename character, so the SDK's own "bin\Debug//**" and
    "obj\Debug//**" patterns match nothing and the exclusion silently does nothing. Adding
    forward-slash patterns to $(DefaultItemExcludes) is necessary but turned out NOT to be
    sufficient here: items pointing into bin still reached _CopyOutOfDateSourceItemsToOutputDirectory
    via _GetCopyToOutputDirectoryItemsFromThisProject, so something other than the default glob
    contributes them.

    The symptom was a web host copying its own output one level deeper on each build —
    bin/Debug/net10.0/bin/Debug/net10.0/... — carrying appsettings.json, deps.json,
    runtimeconfig.json and the staticwebassets manifests down with it. It reached 71 levels and
    161 files before the build failed with MSB3030, unable to copy a runtimeconfig.json out of a
    nested path that no longer contained one.

    Removing by glob at this point is independent of which item group added them, which is why it
    is done here rather than by tightening an exclusion.
  -->
  <Target Name="SankoreStripOutputDirectoryItems" BeforeTargets="AssignTargetPaths">
    <ItemGroup>
      <Content Remove="bin/**" />
      <Content Remove="obj/**" />
      <None Remove="bin/**" />
      <None Remove="obj/**" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
